<div class="card"><h2>13. Automatic fact checks</h2>

<p>When you open a case or a comparison, SICCA compares your description text with the structured data and warns about mismatches, such as a description saying the victims were girls while a male victim is recorded, or a stated victim count that differs from the victims entered. These checks catch typing and copy errors; they do not verify facts against the outside world.</p></div>



<div class="card"><h2>14. Limits and misuse</h2>

<ul><li>Every LR and prior is a human judgment. The output is as good as those judgments and the sources behind them.</li>

<li>Items are only partly independent even with groups; the product can overstate certainty.</li>

<li>Press accounts often copy each other. Ten articles repeating one claim are still one claim: give them one group and an <i>unverified</i> status.</li>

<li>Anchoring risk: once a link feels plausible, it is easy to add supportive items and skip contradicting ones. Record contradictions too.</li>

<li>A low estimate does not prove cases are unrelated, and a high one does not prove they are related. Neither is evidence in a legal sense.</li>

<li>Do not name or accuse individuals on the basis of this score.</li></ul></div>



<div class="card"><h2>15. Glossary</h2>

<table><tr><td>Prior</td><td>Probability before specific evidence.</td></tr><tr><td>Odds</td><td>p / (1 - p). 2% is odds of about 0.02 to 1.</td></tr>

<tr><td>Likelihood ratio</td><td>How much likelier the evidence is if the cases are linked than if not.</td></tr><tr><td>Posterior</td><td>Probability after combining prior and evidence.</td></tr>

<tr><td>Calibration</td><td>Whether stated probabilities match real frequencies.</td></tr><tr><td>Brier score</td><td>Mean squared error between probabilities and outcomes.</td></tr>

<tr><td>Monte Carlo</td><td>Repeated random re-runs to see how results vary with uncertain inputs.</td></tr><tr><td>Base rate</td><td>How often something happens in comparable situations overall.</td></tr></table></div>{% endblock %}"""





